{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966782,"nonce":"251VFTYZdR+r79zLkGBt8GHdbfA=","title":"Canvas overlay paints above the static-cache blit; siblings declared after a canvas in tree","message":"In Blinc's compositor mode (default for windowed apps), the static-layer cache and the canvas overlay are two separate render targets. Each frame:\n1. `composite_frame` blits the static cache onto the surface.\n2. Canvas overlay primitives dispatch with `LoadOp::Load` on top.\n3. Dynamic images + meshes dispatch on top of that.\n\n**Why:** The static cache is rasterized once; you can't interleave content between its z-bands without splitting the cache into multiple textures. Browser compositors solve this with per-layer textures; Blinc currently has a single static texture.\n\n**How to apply (default bg/glass siblings):** If a tree has a canvas followed by stack-layered bg siblings (e.g. `canvas_kit_demo`'s `kit.element()` followed by `viewport_hud` + `reset_button`), the siblings render in the static cache → blitted FIRST → then canvas overlay paints over them. Visual symptom: HUD appears under the canvas, not above.\n\n**Mitigation for foreground siblings (2026-06-04):** `BlincApp::render_foreground_overlay` re-dispatches the static batch's `foreground_primitives` AND `cached_fg_glyphs` AFTER the canvas overlay dispatch at every `composite_frame` callsite. Hosts opt in by marking their above-canvas overlay with `.layer(RenderLayer::Foreground)`. Net order on screen: cache (bg + glass + fg) → canvas overlay → fg overlay. The double-paint of fg pixels (cache + re-dispatch) is identical for opaque content; semi-transparent fg over a canvas will blend twice.\n\n**Text-glyph trap:** Foreground-layer text glyphs do NOT live in `cached_bg_batch.foreground_primitives` — they go to `cached_fg_glyphs` and render via the dedicated text shader (`render_text`), not the SDF PRIM_TEXT path. A re-dispatch that only forwards SDF primitives will paint the HUD's rounded-rect backgrounds above the canvas but leave its TEXT muffled / hidden under the canvas overlay. Always pair `render_primitives_overlay(fg_prims)` with `render_text(cached_fg_glyphs)` for the same z-layer.\n\n`canvas_kit_demo`'s `viewport_hud` / `reset_button` / `reset_button_simple` all carry `.layer(RenderLayer::Foreground)` post-fix as the canonical demo.\n\n**aux_data caveat:** The fg overlay dispatch reuses whatever aux_data the previous pass left in the buffer. Foreground primitives that reference aux entries (3D groups, polygon clip-paths from a fg-layer element) may read stale data. Typical HUD / minimap / toolbar overlays are simple SDF + text and don't reference aux.\n\n`collect_canvas_overlay` sorts canvas paint records by `z_layer` so canvas-vs-canvas ordering within the overlay batch is correct.\n\nStill unfixed for **bg-layer above-canvas siblings**: the only escape hatches are `.layer(RenderLayer::Foreground)` or splitting the static cache. The latter would resolve it for any z-band:\n- Split the static cache into z-banded textures, dispatch canvas overlay between bands\n- Move canvas content into the static cache when there are above-z bg siblings; lose the overlay optimisation for those canvases\n\nSee `crates/blinc_app/src/context.rs` `render_foreground_overlay` + `collect_canvas_overlay` + `try_render_with_compositor` for the current path.\n\n**Datapoint (2026-05-18):** Pre-fix symptom present on desktop windowed runner; user reported the Web version renders canvas_kit_demo's overlays correctly. The Web backend uses a different compositor flow (one render pass per frame, no static-cache split) so the z-ordering naturally follows tree order.","files":null}]}